#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:2
msgid "Using the Secret portal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:4
msgid ""
"The [Secret portal](https://flatpak.github.io/xdg-desktop-portal/docs/doc-"
"org.freedesktop.portal.Secret.html) was designed as a secret storage "
"solution for confined environments, such as snaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:6
msgid ""
"This {ref}`portal<interfaces-xdg-desktop-portals>` allows applications to "
"get a master secret that they can use to encrypt their data. However, it "
"requires a Secret portal backend on the host and a client that knows how to "
"use it. The {ref}`desktop interface<interfaces-desktop-interface>` provides "
"then grants snaps access to the Secret portal API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:8
msgid ""
"In the following  section, we will build a snap to demonstrate a fully "
"working Secret portal example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:10
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:12
msgid ""
"Make sure that your OS supports the secret-portal. `xdg-desktop-portal` "
"version must be equal or greater than 1.5.0. On Ubuntu, it is supported on "
"Ubuntu 20.04 onwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:14
msgid "Building the snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:16
msgid ""
"The most common way to manage secrets in Linux environments is with "
"[libsecret](https://gnome.pages.gitlab.gnome.org/libsecret/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:18
msgid ""
"When an application using libsecret runs unconfined, libsecret uses its "
"*Secret Service* to store/retrieve secrets. However, if libsecrets detects "
"it is being run under confinement (i.e. flatpak or snap), it will use the "
"Secretportal instead. To showcase this behaviour, we are going to build a "
"snap that uses libsecret to manage secrets by packaging the “secret-tool” "
"provided by the libsecret project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:20
msgid ""
"The following is the [snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/"
"snapcraft/stable/reference/project-file/) for our secret-tool snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:22
msgid ""
"name: secret-tool\n"
"version: '0.21.4-1build3'\n"
"summary: secret-tool from libsecret-tools deb.\n"
"description: |\n"
"  command line tool that can be used to store and retrieve passwords.\n"
"\n"
"grade: stable\n"
"confinement: strict\n"
"base: core24\n"
"\n"
"apps:\n"
"  secret-tool:\n"
"    command: usr/bin/secret-tool\n"
"    plugs:\n"
"    - desktop\n"
"\n"
"parts:\n"
"  secret-tool:\n"
"    plugin: nil\n"
"    stage-packages:\n"
"    - libsecret-tools=0.21.4-1build3 \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:46
msgid ""
"The snap can be built with the `snapcraft pack` command. See [Craft a snap]"
"(https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/stable/tutorials/craft-a-snap/) "
"for further details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:48
msgid ""
"When installing the snap, note that , as for the other xdg-desktop-portals, "
"the desktop {ref}`interface must be plugged<how-to-guides-work-with-snaps-"
"connect-interfaces>` to use the secret-portal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:50
msgid "Verifying the behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:52
msgid ""
"Install the secret-tool from the archive (sudo apt install libsecret-tools). "
"We now have two different instances of the secret-tool:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:54
msgid "/usr/bin/secret-tool, which is unconfined"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:55
msgid "/snap/bin/secret-tool, which is confined by the snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:57
msgid ""
"**Check 1:** Create a password with the unconfined instance and verify it is "
"not accessible from the confinement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:59
msgid "Create the password using the unconfined secret-tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:61
msgid ""
"$ /usr/bin/secret-tool store \\--label='My password' origin unconfined  \n"
"Password: 1234  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:66
msgid "Read the password using the unconfined secret-tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:68
msgid ""
"$ /usr/bin/secret-tool lookup origin unconfined  \n"
"1234  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:73
#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:88
msgid "Read the password using the confined secret-tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:75
msgid "$ /snap/bin/secret-tool lookup origin unconfined  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:79
msgid ""
"**Check 2:** Create a password from the snap and verify it is not directly "
"accessible from the outside the confinement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:81
msgid "Create the password using the confined secret-tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:83
msgid ""
"$ /snap/bin/secret-tool store \\--label='My password' origin confined  \n"
"Password: 1234  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:90
msgid ""
"$ /snap/bin/secret-tool lookup origin confined  \n"
"1234  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:95
msgid "Read the password using system secret-tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:97
msgid "$ /usr/bin/secret-tool lookup origin snap  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:101
msgid ""
"**Check 3**: Verify a master secret was created for out secret-tool snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:103
msgid "Read the per-snap encryption password using the unconfined secret-tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:105
msgid ""
"$ /usr/bin/secret-tool lookup app\\_id snap.secret-tool  \n"
"xxxxxxxxxxxxx  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:110
msgid ""
"Support for the Secret portal was added to libsecret in version 0.20.0, "
"however, it was only in version 0.20.5 when snaps started to be supported. "
"This means that most applications using libsecret should use the secret "
"portal out of the box when packaged using core22 and newer bases. It can be "
"verified building the secret-tool snap using different bases and repeating "
"the checks listed in this section. To make it process easier, you can "
"install the secret-tool snap from the store using the appropriate track "
"depending on the base you want to test:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:112
msgid "snap install secret-tool \\--channel XX/stable to use coreXX base  \n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:116
msgid "Electron apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:118
msgid ""
"Electron is a popular framework that's often used to build snaps. Electron "
"applications are recommended to use the [safeStorage](https://"
"www.electronjs.org/docs/latest/api/safe-storage) API to manage secrets, "
"although it cannot currently use the Secret portal. See [https://github.com/"
"jslarraz/snap-secrets-electron](https://github.com/jslarraz/snap-secrets-"
"electron) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:120
msgid ""
"In this case, using safeStorage is still recommended. safeStorage will use "
"the session keyring if the user chooses to connect the password-manager-"
"service interface manually, falling back to plain-text storage otherwise.  "
"Once the underlying libraries (OSCrypt) are able to use the Secret portal, "
"safeStorage will start using it without requiring any changes to the snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:122
msgid "Tauri applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to-guides/snap-development/use-the-secret-portal.md:124
msgid ""
"Tauri applications are increasing in popularity in the snap ecosystem. Tauri "
"as other rust applications can use the secret-portal by using the [Rust "
"bindings for libsecret](https://crates.io/crates/libsecret). Please check "
"[https://github.com/jslarraz/snap-secrets-tauri](https://github.com/jslarraz/"
"snap-secrets-tauri) for a working example."
msgstr ""
